Package: stemflux
Type: Package
Title: Window Selection, Empirical Precision and Detection Limits for
    Chamber Flux Data Processed with 'goFlux'
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Jonathan", "Gewirtzman", email = "jongewirtzman@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Extends the 'goFlux' package (Rheault et al. 2024,
    <doi:10.21105/joss.06393>) with tools developed while processing tree-stem,
    soil and water chamber measurements: stacked multi-gas manual window
    selection, non-interactive window detection from the CO2 rise, windows
    built from notebook times, empirical per-measurement precision (Allan
    deviation of first differences, robust MAD variant, quietest-window scan),
    minimum detectable flux by several published methods with below-detection
    flags, toggleable physical quality screens, a one-call pipeline with
    explicit outputs, a PDF exporter compatible with 'ggplot2' >= 3.5, import
    helpers for very large LI-7810 files, analyzer clock utilities, and an
    opt-in ebullition (bubble) add-on. All functions keep 'goFlux' column
    conventions so they slot into an existing 'goFlux' pipeline.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
